Denornalization:

Normalization
→ Less duplicate data
→ More joins
→ Better write consistency

Denormalization
→ More duplicate data
→ Fewer joins
→ Faster reads
→ More complicated updates


NORMALIZED

Users ──── Orders ──── Products
   \          |           /
    \________ JOIN ______/

More joins
Less duplication


DENORMALIZED

             Orders
    ┌──────────────────────┐
    │ user_name            │ -> Not FK -> directly store in table
    │ product_name         │-> Not FK
    │ price                │
    │ seller_name          │
    │ rating               │
    └──────────────────────┘

Fewer joins
More duplication
Faster reads



Normalization optimizes for data consistency; denormalization optimizes for read performance.





When do we use denormalization?

Commonly in:

Read-heavy applications
High-traffic systems
Distributed databases
NoSQL databases
Search systems like Elasticsearch
CQRS read models - Refer CQRS Patten in this repo

